Privacy policy for notes app:

1. Information We Collect
1.1 Account Information
When you sign in, we collect information required by Firebase Authentication, such as:
Email address (if using email login)
Phone number (if using OTP login)
Google account basic profile (name, email, profile picture — if using Google sign-in)
We do not collect passwords — authentication is handled securely by Firebase.

2. Notes and App Data
Your notes and app data are stored securely in:
✔ Google Firebase Cloud Firestore
The purpose of storing data in the cloud is to:
sync notes across devices
back up notes
restore content when reinstalling
We do not sell or share your content with anyone.

3. How We Use the Information
We use collected information only to:
create and manage your account
store and sync notes
improve app reliability and security
We do not use your information for advertising or tracking.

4. Third-Party Services (Firebase)
This app uses Google Firebase services:
Firebase Authentication
Cloud Firestore
Firebase may collect certain technical information such as:
device information
app usage logs
crash reports
This data is processed according to Google’s privacy policy:

5. Children’s Privacy
This app is intended for all age groups.
We do not knowingly collect more data than necessary to create an account and provide app features.
If a parent believes their child has provided unwanted information, they may contact us and request deletion.

6. Data Sharing
We do not:
✘ sell data ✘ rent data ✘ share data with advertisers ✘ share personal data with third parties except Firebase (service provider)
Data remains connected only to your account.

7. Data Retention and Deletion
Your data remains stored while your account is active.
You may request:
✔ deletion of your account ✔ deletion of your notes
Contact us, and we will delete the data within a reasonable time.

8. Permissions
The app may request permissions only when required for features.
Example:
Internet — to sync with Firebase
Storage (optional, if exporting/importing notes)
Permissions are used only for functionality, not tracking.

9. Security
We rely on Firebase security features including:
encrypted communication (HTTPS)
authentication rules
secure database access controls
However, no system is 100% secure. Use the app responsibly.

10. Changes to This Policy
We may update the Privacy Policy when features change. The latest version will always be available on this page.

